---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import { AgentFanoutList, AgentFanoutPlayground, AgentFanoutStates } from '../../components/AgentFanoutDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Agent Fanout" description="A live tree of the agents a run started and what each one is doing.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Agent Fanout</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    One agent starts others, and they start more. Each agent is a card with its model, tools, task, status, and run
    time. Lines draw in as agents start, and the header counts what is running, needs you, or failed.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <AgentFanoutPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Agent Fanout usage"
      code={`import { AgentFanout } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/agent-fanout";

<AgentFanout
  agent={{
    id: "orchestrator",
    name: "Orchestrator",
    model: "Opus 5.5",
    brand: "claude",
    tools: ["slack", "notion", "github"],
    task: "Launch the new pricing page by Friday",
    status: "running",
    elapsed: 14000,
    agents: [
      {
        id: "researcher",
        name: "Researcher",
        model: "GPT-5.5",
        brand: "openai",
        tools: ["notion", "slack"],
        task: "Compare the pricing of five competitors",
        status: "running",
        elapsed: 7000,
      },
    ],
  }}
  onRetry={retry}
  onDismiss={dismiss}
  onOpen={open}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass the agent that started the run as <code>agent</code>, and the agents it started as its <code>agents</code>,
      as deep as they go. Your app owns the run: move each <code>status</code> through <code>queued</code>,{' '}
      <code>running</code>, <code>needs-you</code>, <code>done</code>, <code>failed</code>, and <code>stopped</code>,
      and tick <code>elapsed</code> in ms.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>brand</code> picks the model's logo from Brand Icon, and <code>model</code> names it. Pass <code>icon</code>{' '}
      for agents that are not a known model. <code>tools</code> are Brand Icon names; past four, the last shows as a
      count.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Needs you and failed</h2>
    <p>
      Agents that need you or failed get a button in the header. It opens a list with each agent's task and{' '}
      <code>reason</code>. Pass <code>onOpen</code> to add Open to agents that need you, and <code>onRetry</code> and{' '}
      <code>onDismiss</code> to add Retry and Dismiss to failed ones. The component does not change the run itself. In
      the demo above, Retry stops the failed agent and starts a new one, and Dismiss stops it.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <AgentFanoutStates client:visible />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Layout</h2>
    <p>
      The agents the root starts sit side by side, joined by one line. Deeper agents stack under their parent. With{' '}
      <code>layout="auto"</code>, the default, the tree turns into a list when the row does not fit, so every agent
      stacks under its parent. Set <code>layout="list"</code> to always stack, or <code>layout="tree"</code> to always
      use a row and scroll sideways.
    </p>
    <p>
      The number in a card's footer shows or hides the agents it started. Pass <code>defaultCollapsed</code> with agent
      ids to start them hidden.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <AgentFanoutList client:visible />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Motion</h2>
    <p>
      A new agent's line draws from its parent, then its card fades in. Other cards slide to make room, status badges
      swap in, and header counts roll. Hidden or removed cards fade out where they stood while their lines retract.
      Nothing animates on first load. With reduced motion, cards and lines only fade and the running spinner stops.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The tree is a nested list, labeled by who started each level, so screen readers hear its depth. Lines are hidden
      from them. Each footer button says what it does, such as “Hide 3 agents started by Orchestrator”, and reports
      whether its list is open. One live status reads the header counts when they change. Run times are{' '}
      <code>&lt;time&gt;</code> elements and stay quiet.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Cards use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>, and <code>--sprout-radius-panel</code>, like
      Card. Statuses use the Badge colors. Lines use <code>--sprout-agent-fanout-line</code>, a neutral mix of{' '}
      <code>--sprout-border-strong</code> and <code>--sprout-line</code>. Lines leading to running agents use{' '}
      <code>--sprout-agent-fanout-line-active</code>, a mix of <code>--sprout-info</code>. Set{' '}
      <code>--sprout-agent-fanout-card</code> (17.25rem), <code>--sprout-agent-fanout-gap</code> (3rem), and{' '}
      <code>--sprout-agent-fanout-indent</code> (2.5rem) to change the card width, the space between side-by-side cards,
      and how far stacked agents indent.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
